on services division."},"products":[],"endMarkets":"India (Hindi and regional-language film markets)","currentContext":{"business":"The Company is engaged in the business of Production and Distribution of films, web-series and related content, and operates in a single business segment (Films). It owns the copyrights to its film library and monetizes it across mediums such as Satellite, OTT, etc., and also has a third-party theatrical distribution services division.","products":{},"end_markets":{},"plants":{},"promoters":{},"board":{},"related":{},"strengths":{},"strategies":{},"expansion":"The Company is building a project pipeline to sustain 5 to 6 film productions per year. Currently 3 films are on the floor, with one joint production being explored with a leading production house. Its third-party theatrical distribution services division is gradually scaling up — it has distributed Sikandar and Housefull 5, and handled the entire distribution of its own film Hai Jawani Toh Ishq Hona Hai in-house, with this activity expected to scale up further.","mdna":{},"risks":{},"as_of":"","concallIntel":{}},"topics":{"one_liner":{"title":"One Liner (RHP)","body":"TIPS Films Limited is engaged in the production and distribution of films, web-series and related content, monetizing an owned film library across mediums such as Satellite and OTT.","src":"drhp","as_of":""},"business_model":{"title":"Business (RHP)","body":"The Company is engaged in the business of Production and Distribution of films, web-series and related content, and operates in a single business segment (Films). It owns the copyrights to its film library and monetizes it across mediums such as Satellite, OTT, etc., and also has a third-party theatrical distribution services division.","src":"drhp","as_of":""},"group_structure":{"title":"Related (RHP)","body":"[{\"name\": \"Tips Music Limited\", \"relation\": \"related party\", \"note\": \"Group Company; Mr. Kumar S. Taurani is Chairman & Managing Director and Mr. Ramesh S. Taurani is Executive Director of Tips Music Limited; shareholders approved continuation of related-party contracts/arrangements/transactions …","src":"drhp","as_of":""},"end_markets":{"title":"End Markets (RHP)","body":"India (Hindi and regional-language film markets)","src":"drhp","as_of":""},"demand_drivers":{"title":"Mdna (RHP)","body":"- The state of the film industry remains very healthy and the outlook on content demand is positive.\n- M&E industry is poised for significant growth, driven by digital transformation and a growing consumer base.\n- Growth expected to be driven by increased theatrical revenues, films incorporating more VFX to enhance the movie-going experience, and continued growth in screen counts in untapped geographies.\n- The film release slate for 2026 appears strong, with several mass films, a larger star cast than in 2025 and increased special effects.\n- Untapped OTT-led monetization avenues and growing demand for …","src":"drhp","as_of":""},"capex_expansion":{"title":"Expansion (RHP)","body":"The Company is building a project pipeline to sustain 5 to 6 film productions per year. Currently 3 films are on the floor, with one joint production being explored with a leading production house. Its third-party theatrical distribution services division is gradually scaling up — it has distributed Sikandar and Housefull 5, and handled the entire distribution of its own film Hai Jawani Toh Ishq Hona Hai in-house, with this activity expected to scale up further.","src":"drhp","as_of":""},"moat":{"title":"Strengths (RHP)","body":"distribution: A valuable and expanding content library across Hindi and regional-language titles — evidence: the AR names an owned library including Raja Hindustani, Raaz, Race, Ajab Prem ki Ghazab Kahani and others, with the Company holding copyrights and its film Legend of Bhagat Singh having won the National Award for Best Feature Film in Hindi.","src":"drhp","as_of":""},"risks":{"title":"Risks (RHP)","body":"- The Company requires statutory and regulatory permits and approvals for its business and may need further approvals/renewals in future; there is no assurance these will be issued in the anticipated timeframe, and failure to do so may interrupt operations and materially affect business, financial condition and results.\n- Demand for filmed content depends substantially on consumer tastes and preferences that change unpredictably; there is no formula to predict whether a given film will succeed, so business success depends on consistently meeting changing preferences.\n- A significant portion of revenues is derived from theatrical box office sales, particularly in a film's first week; poor box office receipts could adversely affect results both in the year of release and in future revenues expected from other distribution channels.\n- The business is highly dependent on maintaining intellectual property rights; piracy, including digital/internet piracy, may decrease revenue from exploitation of the Company's products, and consumer awareness of piracy consequences is lower in India than in Western countries.\n- Film production is exposed to budget overruns due to unforeseen factors.\n- Filming on locations can be unpredictable; rain, wind and extreme temperatures can cause delays in filming.\n- Films face intense competition at the time of release, and films and traditional media are competing for finite human attention against fast-form entertainment.\n- Hackers stealing unreleased scripts, leaking footage, or launching cyber attacks can ruin a project before it reaches theatres.","src":"drhp","as_of":""},"strategy":{"title":"Strategies (RHP)","body":"- Focus on identifying high quality and economically viable film scripts, given artist compensation is the key factor making film projects unviable.\n- Scale up the third-party theatrical distribution services division, alongside in-house distribution of the Company's own films.\n- Explore joint productions with leading production houses.\n- Geared up for 5 to 6 productions per year, building a project pipeline to achieve this target.\n- Monetize the owned film library across mediums such as Satellite, OTT, etc.","src":"drhp","as_of":""}},"scorecard":{"symbol":"TIPSFILMS","fin_source":"shadow ledger (per-field legacy fallback)","fy_asof":"2026-03-31","opm_basis":"TTM 4q","opm_ttm":"-80.92500000000001","roe":"-42.09","roce":"-6.95","bq_a":"0","sales_cagr_3y":"37.075205312326354","eps_cagr_3y":"","bq_b":"10","debt_equity":"6.300100368016059","interest_cover":"-20.226666666666667","bq_c":"0","cfo_pat_3y":"","wc_basis":"WC/sales trend","bq_d":"5","share_cagr_3y":"-0.023137437197928712","bq_e":"6","shp_asof":"2026-06-30","promoter_pct":"74.98","promoter_prev":"74.98","pledge_basis":"pledge not in snapshot -> 0 penalty (hook)","piotroski_basis":"needs 2 FYs of BS_* -> 0 (real from FY27)","bq_f":"5","g_integrity":"5","g_execution":"0","g_capalloc":"0","g_basis":"defaults (no WTT/ledger coverage)","bq_g":"5","bq_total":"31","bq_gate":"False","stage2":"False","sector_on":"False","market_on":"True","rs_rank":"","per_a":"5","pe_ttm":"","pe_basis":"TTM trailing (spec band written for forward P/E)","per_b":"0","earn_accel":"DECEL","rev_accel":"NEUTRAL","per_c":"0","per_d":"6","per_e":"0","per_total":"11","per_gate":"False","advt_rs":"","full_position_eligible":"False","verdict":"OBSERVE","notes":""},"concallIntel":{},"segments":[],"themes":[],"ipo":{"summary":{},"analysis":{}},"coverage":{"concall":false,"deepDive":false,"drhp":true,"projection":false,"stage":false},"pageModel":{"schemaVersion":"company-page/1.0","layout":"vertical","identity":{"symbol":"TIPSFILMS","name":"TIPS FILMS LIMITED","sector":"Media, Entertainment & Publication","industry":"Entertainment"},"coverage":{"deepDive":false,"drhp":true,"stage":false,"priceHistory":true,"themes":false,"concall":false},"adapters":{"deepDive":{"available":false,"profile":"none","sections":{}},"drhp":{"available":true,"structured":true,"profi